values.content:
=A student from class {{ $json.subject }} has submitted a {{ $json.difficulty }} question.

Classification context:
- Subject: {{ $json.subject }}
- Chapter: {{ $json.chapter }}
- Topic: {{ $json.topic }}
- Keywords detected: {{ $json.keywords.join(', ') }}

Question to solve:
{{ $json.questionText }}

Solve the question completely. Then decide whether a diagram would genuinely help the student understand the solution better. If yes, populate the appropriate spec with real, question-specific values — not placeholders.

Return this exact JSON and nothing else:

{
  "summary": "<b>One-line summary</b> of what the question is asking.",
  "solution": "Step 1: ...\nStep 2: ...\nStep 3: ...",
  "final_answer": "Plain text or <code>expression</code>.",
  "confidence_score": 0,
  "confidence_reason": "One-line reason.",

  "diagram_needed": true | false,
  "diagram_type": null | "circuit" | "graph" | "waveform" | "geometric" | "phasor",

  "circuit_spec": null | {
    "title": "string",
    "elements": [
      {
        "type": "resistor|capacitor|inductor|opamp|ground|wire|source_v|source_i|diode|bjt_npn|bjt_pnp|mosfet_n|mosfet_p|dot|switch|move",
        "direction": "right|left|up|down",
        "label": "e.g. R1 = 10Ω",
        "length": 2,
        "name": "optional — saves this node for reuse with at:",
        "at": "optional — jumps drawing cursor to a saved node"
      }
    ]
  },

  "graph_spec": null | {
    "type": "graph|waveform|geometric|phasor",
    "title": "string",
    "xlabel": "string",
    "ylabel": "string",
    "xrange": [min, max],
    "yrange": [min, max],
    "curves": [
      { "expr": "numpy expression using x, e.g. np.sin(2*x)", "label": "string", "color": "blue", "style": "-" }
    ],
    "points": [
      { "x": 0, "y": 0, "label": "string", "color": "red" }
    ],
    "lines": [
      { "axis": "x|y", "value": 0, "style": "--", "color": "gray", "label": "string" }
    ],
    "regions": [
      { "x1": 0, "x2": 1, "color": "yellow", "alpha": 0.3, "label": "string" }
    ],
    "annotations": [
      { "text": "string", "x": 0, "y": 0, "tx": 0.5, "ty": 0.5 }
    ],
    "shapes": [
      { "type": "circle|polygon|arrow|line_segment|point" }
    ]
  }
}

Spec rules:
- Populate circuit_spec ONLY when diagram_type = "circuit". Otherwise null.
- Populate graph_spec ONLY when diagram_type is "graph", "waveform", "geometric", or "phasor". Otherwise null.
- All values in specs must be derived from the actual question — no generic placeholders.
- curve expr must be valid numpy: use np.sin(x), x**2, np.exp(-0.5*x), etc.
- waveform questions: use graph_spec with type "waveform" and set frequency + amplitude from the question.
- geometric questions: use graph_spec with type "geometric" and draw the figure using shapes + points + lines.
- phasor questions: use graph_spec with type "phasor" and represent each phasor as an arrow shape with correct magnitude and angle.

